WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:08.241
NARRATOR: Thomas and
Jennifer are investigating

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:10.844
one of Tutankhamun's secrets.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.847
Excavating under a ruined
fortress for evidence

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:19.018
he got his gold from the
inhospitable Eastern desert.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.287
Did his miners shelter here?

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:27.360
The team has just
found something.

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:29.629
Stone blocks that
offer a tantalizing

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:32.532
glimpse of a settlement
from Tutankhamun's time.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.337
So these are
architectural blocks.

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:41.040
They carry some hieroglyphic
inscription very faintly

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:44.711
visible here, which would
indicate that they were carved

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:47.113
and set up in some sort
of building which dates

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.215
to the reign of Tutankhamun.

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:50.617
It's exciting,
because that gives us

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.652
a sort of a ballpark
for the time when

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:55.722
this site was busy and
active and important

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:58.458
during the 18th dynasty.

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:01.795
NARRATOR: Jennifer's team must
now move the precious blocks

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:04.998
offsite for further analysis.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:09.002
As they dig deeper into the
layers below the fortress,

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:11.871
they uncover more clues
that this site was

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:13.873
in use in Tutankhamun's time.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.242
JENNIFER GATES-FOSTER:
It is beautiful.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:21.815
This is a really distinctive,
very different from any

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.751
of the Ptolemaic material,
the Greek style pottery

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:27.654
that we find in most of
the rooms of the Fort

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.522
that is really common.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:32.659
This kind of pottery, which
belongs to the New Kingdom,

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.093
is not wheel made.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.562
It's handmade, and
you can tell that

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:38.298
by looking at the
interior of the pot, which

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:41.000
has a surface which
is very irregular

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:45.371
and that it's been smoothed
with a smooth stone most likely.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.173
NARRATOR: It's not
just one or two pieces

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.542
of Tutankhamun-era pottery.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.845
Jennifer's team is
revealing that the layers

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.914
of Earth beneath the fortress
are packed full of it.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:56.282
JENNIFER GATES-FOSTER:
We have New

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:58.151
Kingdom material
under the floors of

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:01.821
rooms 20, 19, 26, 18, and 17.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:05.558
But to have the Fort now
documented on top of deposits

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:08.261
that indicates some kind of
occupation in the New Kingdom

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:11.564
and that's really exciting.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.967
NARRATOR: The discovery
is proof the site

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.569
may have been used
in Tutankhamun's time

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.171
by his gold workers.

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:21.074
But the team have found
another remarkable clue

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.409
concealed in the fortress.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:28.548
Cutting into the bedrock 60 feet
below the surface is a well.

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:30.617
It's a vital source
of water that

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:34.854
explains why the safe haven
and Tutankhamun's gold workers

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.756
were here.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:39.359
THOMAS FAUCHER: The well was
built the time of Tutankhamun

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.960
by the evidence we have now.

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:45.632
It was, I guess, more precious
than even than gold for people

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:51.271
that they can have water
to go inside the desert.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.673
NARRATOR: The evidence
here and at other sites

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.242
reveals how Tutankhamun
got his gold

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:57.944
from the remote Eastern desert.

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:05.118
Miners had to trek
vast distances

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:08.588
from the Nile Valley
across the hot, dry desert

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:09.822
to reach the gold mines.

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:15.862
Ancient engineers dug
wells along the route

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:17.630
for precious drinking water.

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:25.305
Each well was a day's
walk from the last,

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:28.207
creating a network
of vital rest stops.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:35.582
This allowed them to
survive the brutal journey

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:38.651
across the desert to
mine gold in the East

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.420
and bring it back
to their Pharaoh.

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:48.261
Thomas and Jennifer
have revealed

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:51.598
one of Tutankhamun's secrets.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:55.201
Sites like this were a critical
part of the infrastructure that

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:58.104
allowed him to amass the
gold for one of the most

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:00.873
elaborate burials in history.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.942
JENNIFER GATES-FOSTER:
The gold in Tut's masks,

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:04.444
all that gold in
his tomb, that's

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.145
coming from the Eastern desert.

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:08.915
So sites like this that
looked really modest

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:11.117
are actually the
mechanism that allowed

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:14.187
New Kingdom gold to be mined.

